    outline: [{"level":1,"text":"Complex Numbers","id":"complex-numbers"},{"level":1,"text":"BASIC DEFINITION","id":"basic-definition"},{"level":1,"text":"MODULUS AND ARGUMENT","id":"modulus-and-argument"},{"level":1,"text":"CONJUGATE","id":"conjugate"},{"level":1,"text":"POLAR FORM","id":"polar-form"},{"level":1,"text":"EULER FORM","id":"euler-form"},{"level":1,"text":"MULTIPLICATION & DIVISION (POLAR)","id":"multiplication-division-polar"},{"level":1,"text":"DE MOIVRE’S THEOREM","id":"de-moivres-theorem"},{"level":1,"text":"ROOTS OF COMPLEX NUMBERS","id":"roots-of-complex-numbers"},{"level":1,"text":"GEOMETRIC INTERPRETATION","id":"geometric-interpretation"},{"level":1,"text":"IMPORTANT IDENTITIES","id":"important-identities"},{"level":1,"text":"STANDARD RESULTS","id":"standard-results"},{"level":1,"text":"ARGUMENT PROPERTIES","id":"argument-properties"},{"level":1,"text":"LOCUS (IMPORTANT)","id":"locus-important"},{"level":1,"text":"EXPONENTIAL FORM (ADVANCED USE)","id":"exponential-form-advanced-use"},{"level":1,"text":"IMPORTANT TRICKS (LEEE FOCUS)","id":"important-tricks-leee-focus"},{"level":1,"text":"CORE FORMULAS SUMMARY","id":"core-formulas-summary"},{"level":1,"text":"Questions","id":"questions"},{"level":1,"text":"References","id":"references"}],
    content: `# Complex Numbers 

---

# BASIC DEFINITION

- A complex number:
  $$z = a + ib$$

- Real part: $\\operatorname{Re}(z) = a$  
- Imaginary part: $\\operatorname{Im}(z) = b$

- $i = \\sqrt{-1}$, with:
  - $i^2 = -1$
  - $i^3 = -i$
  - $i^4 = 1$ (cycle repeats)

---

# MODULUS AND ARGUMENT

- Modulus:
  $$|z| = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}$$

- Argument:
  $\\arg(z) = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{b}{a}\\right)$ (adjust quadrant)

---

# CONJUGATE

- Conjugate:
  $$\\overline{z} = a - ib$$

- Important results:
  - $z \\cdot \\overline{z} = |z|^2$
  - $|z_1 z_2| = |z_1||z_2|$
  - $\\overline{z_1 z_2} = \\overline{z_1} \\cdot \\overline{z_2}$

---

# POLAR FORM

- $$z = r(\\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta)$$
  where $r = |z|$, $\\theta = \\arg(z)$

---

# EULER FORM

- $$z = re^{i\\theta}$$

- $$e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta$$

---

# MULTIPLICATION & DIVISION (POLAR)

- Multiplication:
  $$z_1 z_2 = r_1 r_2 \\, \\text{cis}(\\theta_1 + \\theta_2)$$

- Division:
  $$\\frac{z_1}{z_2} = \\frac{r_1}{r_2} \\, \\text{cis}(\\theta_1 - \\theta_2)$$

---

# DE MOIVRE’S THEOREM

- $$[r(\\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta)]^n = r^n (\\cos n\\theta + i\\sin n\\theta)$$

---

# ROOTS OF COMPLEX NUMBERS

- $$z^{1/n} = r^{1/n} \\, \\text{cis}\\left(\\frac{\\theta + 2k\\pi}{n}\\right), \\quad k = 0,1,...,n-1$$

---

# GEOMETRIC INTERPRETATION

- Complex number ↔ point $(a,b)$ in plane  
- $|z|$ = distance from origin  

---

# IMPORTANT IDENTITIES

- $$|z_1 + z_2| \\le |z_1| + |z_2|$$  (Triangle inequality)

- $|z_1 - z_2| \\ge ||z_1| - |z_2||$

---

# STANDARD RESULTS

- If $|z| = 1$, then:
  - $z\\overline{z} = 1$

- If $z = x + iy$:
  - $|z|^2 = x^2 + y^2$

---

# ARGUMENT PROPERTIES

- $\\arg(z_1 z_2) = \\arg z_1 + \\arg z_2$

- $\\arg\\left(\\frac{z_1}{z_2}\\right) = \\arg z_1 - \\arg z_2$

---

# LOCUS (IMPORTANT)

- $|z - z_0| = r$ → circle  
- $|z - z_1| = |z - z_2|$ → perpendicular bisector  

---

# EXPONENTIAL FORM (ADVANCED USE)

- $$e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta$$

- $$\\cos\\theta = \\frac{e^{i\\theta} + e^{-i\\theta}}{2}$$

- $$\\sin\\theta = \\frac{e^{i\\theta} - e^{-i\\theta}}{2i}$$

---

# IMPORTANT TRICKS (LEEE FOCUS)

- Multiply by conjugate to simplify division  
- Convert to polar form for powers/roots  
- Use geometry for locus questions  

---

# CORE FORMULAS SUMMARY

- $$z = a + ib$$

- $$|z| = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}$$

- $$z = r(\\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta)$$

- $$e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta$$

- $$[r(\\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta)]^n = r^n(\\cos n\\theta + i\\sin n\\theta)$$
---
# Questions








---
# References`
