    content: `# BASIC RATIOS

- $\\sin\\theta = \\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$
- $\\cos\\theta = \\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$
- $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$

- $\\csc\\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta}$
- $\\sec\\theta = \\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta}$
- $\\cot\\theta = \\frac{1}{\\tan\\theta}$

---

# FUNDAMENTAL IDENTITIES

- $$\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$$
- $$1 + \\tan^2\\theta = \\sec^2\\theta$$
- $$1 + \\cot^2\\theta = \\csc^2\\theta$$

---

# STANDARD VALUES

| $\\theta$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ |
|----------|-----|----------------|----------------|----------------|----------------|
| $\\sin\\theta$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $1$ |
| $\\cos\\theta$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ |
| $\\tan\\theta$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $1$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | undefined |
| $\\csc\\theta$ | undefined | $2$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $1$ |
| $\\sec\\theta$ | $1$ | $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $2$ | undefined |
| $\\cot\\theta$ | undefined | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $0$ |

---

# COMPOUND ANGLE FORMULAS

- $$\\sin(A \\pm B) = \\sin A \\cos B \\pm \\cos A \\sin B$$
- $$\\cos(A \\pm B) = \\cos A \\cos B \\mp \\sin A \\sin B$$
- $$\\tan(A \\pm B) = \\frac{\\tan A \\pm \\tan B}{1 \\mp \\tan A \\tan B}$$

---

# DOUBLE ANGLE FORMULAS

- $$\\sin 2\\theta = 2\\sin\\theta \\cos\\theta$$
- $$\\cos 2\\theta = \\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta$$
- $\\cos 2\\theta = 2\\cos^2\\theta - 1$
- $\\cos 2\\theta = 1 - 2\\sin^2\\theta$
- $$\\tan 2\\theta = \\frac{2\\tan\\theta}{1 - \\tan^2\\theta}$$

---

# HALF ANGLE FORMULAS

- $\\sin^2\\frac{\\theta}{2} = \\frac{1 - \\cos\\theta}{2}$
- $\\cos^2\\frac{\\theta}{2} = \\frac{1 + \\cos\\theta}{2}$

- $$\\tan\\frac{\\theta}{2} = \\frac{1 - \\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}$$
- $$\\tan\\frac{\\theta}{2} = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1 + \\cos\\theta}$$

---

# PRODUCT TO SUM

- $\\sin A \\sin B = \\frac{1}{2}[\\cos(A-B) - \\cos(A+B)]$
- $\\cos A \\cos B = \\frac{1}{2}[\\cos(A-B) + \\cos(A+B)]$
- $\\sin A \\cos B = \\frac{1}{2}[\\sin(A+B) + \\sin(A-B)]$

---

# SUM TO PRODUCT

- $\\sin A + \\sin B = 2 \\sin\\frac{A+B}{2} \\cos\\frac{A-B}{2}$
- $\\cos A + \\cos B = 2 \\cos\\frac{A+B}{2} \\cos\\frac{A-B}{2}$

---

# TRIGONOMETRIC EQUATIONS

- $\\sin\\theta = \\sin\\alpha \\Rightarrow \\theta = n\\pi + (-1)^n \\alpha$
- $\\cos\\theta = \\cos\\alpha \\Rightarrow \\theta = 2n\\pi \\pm \\alpha$
- $\\tan\\theta = \\tan\\alpha \\Rightarrow \\theta = n\\pi + \\alpha$

---

# TRIGONOMETRIC INEQUALITIES

- $\\sin\\theta > 0 \\Rightarrow \\theta \\in (0,\\pi)$
- $\\cos\\theta > 0 \\Rightarrow \\theta \\in (-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2})$
- $\\tan\\theta > 0 \\Rightarrow \\theta \\in (0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\cup (\\pi,\\frac{3\\pi}{2})$

---

# SMALL ANGLE APPROXIMATIONS

- $\\sin\\theta \\approx \\theta$
- $\\tan\\theta \\approx \\theta$
- $\\cos\\theta \\approx 1 - \\frac{\\theta^2}{2}$

---

# INVERSE TRIGONOMETRY

- $\\sin^{-1}x + \\cos^{-1}x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$
- $\\tan^{-1}x + \\cot^{-1}x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$

---

# TRIANGLE FORMULAS

## Sine Rule
$$
\\frac{a}{\\sin A} = \\frac{b}{\\sin B} = \\frac{c}{\\sin C}
$$

## Cosine Rule
$$
c^2 = a^2 + b^2 - 2ab\\cos C
$$

## Area using trig
$$
\\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C
$$

---

# IMPORTANT RESULTS

## Periodicity
- $\\sin(\\theta + 2\\pi) = \\sin\\theta$
- $\\cos(\\theta + 2\\pi) = \\cos\\theta$
- $\\tan(\\theta + \\pi) = \\tan\\theta$

## Even-Odd Properties
- $\\sin(-\\theta) = -\\sin\\theta$
- $\\cos(-\\theta) = \\cos\\theta$
- $\\tan(-\\theta) = -\\tan\\theta$

## Complementary Angles
- $\\sin(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\cos\\theta$
- $\\cos(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\sin\\theta$
- $\\tan(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\cot\\theta$

---

# MAX-MIN RESULT

- $$a\\sin\\theta + b\\cos\\theta \\le \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}$$

---

# CORE FORMULAS SUMMARY

- $$\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$$
- $$\\sin(A \\pm B) = \\sin A \\cos B \\pm \\cos A \\sin B$$
- $$\\cos(A \\pm B) = \\cos A \\cos B \\mp \\sin A \\sin B$$
- $$\\sin 2\\theta = 2\\sin\\theta \\cos\\theta$$
- $$\\cos 2\\theta = 1 - 2\\sin^2\\theta$$
- $$\\tan 2\\theta = \\frac{2\\tan\\theta}{1 - \\tan^2\\theta}$$

---

## 🔗 Connections

- cos(A±B) formula is the basis for ArcFace decision boundary cos(θ+m) → [[ArcFace]]
- Angular margin in face embeddings applies compound angle formulas → [[Face Embedding]]
- CosFace loss function uses additive cosine margin → [[Face Embedding]]`
